    "title": "105: Session hooks for hosts: a brief at session start, mention routing at the prompt, and a marker at the end"
  },
  "summary": {
    "kind": "quote",
    "span": {
      "end": 2244,
      "end_line": 26,
      "line": 26,
      "start": 1812
    },
    "text": "Today everything that makes a host session a Delphi session depends on the host's model remembering to do it: look at the specs, know the roster, notice `@name`, leave a summary. This spec moves the parts that need no judgement into three hooks, so the model starts each session already knowing who is on the team, what the project's specs say and what the last session left, and so `@name` works without a skill having to match it."
  }
